theta_e,point,*,g_bar,given,,,,fraction,x_strong_lensing_theta_e_err_frac_hi,as_released,a6s_theta_e,,not_published,"R5 (Bolton et al. 2008); R20 (Sonnenfeld et al. 2013a); R32 (Smith et al. 2020); R29 (Collier, Smith & Lucey 2018b)","R5 ms_arxiv.tex l. 972–975; R20 sl2s-rm-pdflatex.tex l. 462, 477–478; R32 main.tex l. 176, l. 261; R29 newlens.tex l. 196","§2a rule 7, class A rows only (rule 5); the column is empty elsewhere, including NGC 6505. Moves g_bar and the coordinate R_E; g_obs = π G Σ_cr is unchanged. Two-sided: x_strong_lensing_theta_e_err_frac_lo holds the other side. SLACS: R5's adopted ""2% RMS fractional error"" (ms_arxiv.tex l. 972–975), no level stated (""RMS"" names a statistic, not a confidence level); R13 used ""a conservative 5%"" for its lensing masses only (plain.txt l. 1669–1671); R13 does not state that its M* errors include the θ_E error (v2 reading). R9 0.5 % (ms_v2.tex l. 138) and SL2S's 3 % in this note (F3). SL2S: R20's 68 % intervals including its 3 % systematic (sl2s-rm-pdflatex.tex l. 462, 477–478). MaNGA: R32 l. 176 and l. 261 (J1701: 10 per cent as stated; Table 1 prints 1.63 ± 0.16). J0403: ±0.03″ of 1.47″ (R29 l. 196). The a6s_theta_e formula is first order in ln θ_E; at J1701's 10 % the second-order term is not computed, and where no light profile is printed the effect on g_bar is not computed (D-104 rule 3)",
theta_e_ngc6505,point,aeg-s-000509,g_bar,given,0.0004,,,fraction,,lower_bound,a6s_theta_e,,not_published,R30 (O'Riordan et al. 2025),ms.tex l. 798; θ_E l. 813,"0.001″ of 2.500″. ""should therefore be considered lower-bounds which only account for measurement uncertainty"" (R30 ms.tex l. 798; θ_E l. 813). The θ_E effect is not computed where no profile is printed (rule 5)",
ellipticity_j0403,point,*,g_obs,given,,,,fraction,x_strong_lensing_mass_ellipticity_frac,as_released,,,not_published,"R29 (Collier, Smith & Lucey 2018b)",newlens.tex l. 210,"One-sided, upward; J0403−0239 only. ""Including a small ellipticity (e ≈ 0.1 as measured from galfit) increases the mass by 3 per cent"" (R29 newlens.tex l. 210); a change in M_E at fixed radius. R29's revised ""∼4 per cent"" total is not used, to avoid counting the 2 % θ_E part twice",no
