cosmology_h0_snells,dataset,aeg-s-000503;aeg-s-000504;aeg-s-000505,g_obs,given,,67.0,70.0,km s-1 Mpc-1,,range,a6s_source_cosmology,,not_published,"R25 (Smith, Lucey & Conroy 2015)",snellsI_arxiv.tex l. 862–863; l. 188,"p = 67/70, from the term's own pair (applying D-094/D-104). ""Adopting $H_0$ = 67 … from the Planck cosmology (Planck Collaboration 2014), rather than … 70 … from WMAP7"" (R25 snellsI_arxiv.tex l. 862–863). R25 adopts 70.4 (l. 188); the pair is R25's own comparison, 67 against 70 (v2 reading, resolution 5). v1's rows carry 70.4 (WMAP7, R28 and R61), which does not enter p. In α: ""would yield smaller α by ∼5 per cent"" (l. 863)",
cosmology_h0_j0403,dataset,aeg-s-000506,g_obs,given,,67.8,70.4,km s-1 Mpc-1,,range,a6s_source_cosmology,,not_published,"R29 (Collier, Smith & Lucey 2018b); Planck Collaboration 2016, A&A 594, A13 (arXiv 1502.01589)","newlens.tex l. 210, l. 241","p = 67.8/70.4 (applying D-094/D-104). Adopted 70.4 (R29 l. 210). Alternative: ""If we had prescribed the [Planck Collaboration 2016] cosmology"" (l. 241); that paper is A&A 594, A13 (arXiv 1502.01589), whose abstract gives ""H0= (67.8 +/- 0.9) km/s/Mpc"". In α: ""4 per cent lower, due to the variation in H0"" (l. 241)",
cosmology_h0_manga,dataset,aeg-s-000507;aeg-s-000508,g_obs,given,,67.4,69.6,km s-1 Mpc-1,,range,a6s_source_cosmology,,not_published,"R32 (Smith et al. 2020); Planck Collaboration 2018 (arXiv 1807.06209); Bennett et al. 2014, ApJ 794, 135 (arXiv 1406.1718)","main.tex l. 100–101, l. 293","p = 69.6/67.4 (applying D-094/D-104). Adopted: ""We adopt the cosmological parameters from"" Planck Collaboration 2018 (R32 main.tex l. 100–101); arXiv 1807.06209 abstract: ""$H_0 = (67.4\pm 0.5)$km/s/Mpc"". Alternative: Bennett et al. 2014 (l. 293); arXiv 1406.1718 abstract: ""69.6+/-0.7 km/s/Mpc"". v1's MaNGA rows have no x_strong_lensing_h0, which does not enter p. In α: ""would increase α by 3.5 per cent"" (l. 293)",
