lens_distance_snl0,system,aeg-s-000503,g_obs,given,,0.03,0.04,fraction of D_l,,as_released,a6s_lens_distance,,not_published,R26 (Newman et al. 2017),snells.tex l. 139,"""an uncertainty corresponding to a 500 km s⁻¹ peculiar velocity (3-4%)"" (R26 snells.tex l. 139), stated for the lensing M/L, which R26 states is proportional to distance; applied as a shift of ±size_hi in D_l (a6s_lens_distance, which assumes D_s ≫ D_l). In α: ""up to 5 per cent"" (R25 l. 864); R28: ""rescaling the distance assumed for [ESO 325-G004] affects $\alpha_{\rm MW}$ linearly"" (lensz_arXiv.tex l. 727–730), an α statement (v2 reading)",
