lens_distance_ngc6505,system,aeg-s-000509,g_obs,given,,0.04,0.04243,redshift,,range,a6s_lens_distance,,not_published,R30 (O'Riordan et al. 2025),ms.tex l. 639; l. 790,"z 0.04243 (spectroscopic, l. 639) against 0.041 ± 0.001 (cosmological). ""On top of the bulk flow peculiar velocities of individual galaxies are typically present at the $150\,\kms$ level. Combining these two effects results in a cosmological redshift of $z=0.041\pm0.001$"" (R30 ms.tex l. 790). R30 does not state which one it uses for distances (v2 reading 3.7). Effect not computed in v2 (applying D-094/D-104). v1's alternative row (z = 0.041) stays as it is",
